From: Nick Schuetz <nschuetz@redhat.com>
Subject: [PATCH] PhysX/PAL: gate poly2tri ly_associate_package on LY_USE_SYSTEM_POLY2TRI

Stage 1 system-library swap for poly2tri. The audit at
2026-05-07 (issue #7) found:

  - Engine consumes poly2tri exclusively within Gems/PhysX/Core/
    (zero references in Code/). Specifically, only
    Gems/PhysX/Core/Code/Editor/PolygonPrismMeshUtils.h (an
    editor-only utility for triangulating 2D polygons for
    polygon-prism shape colliders).
  - Engine uses public p2t:: namespace API only (p2t::Point,
    p2t::Triangle, etc.); no internal-namespace symbols.
  - Fedora 44 ships poly2tri-devel as a system package, from
    Mason Green's original BSD-3-Clause upstream
    (commit 26242d0a, May 2013). License-clean; independent of
    O3DE bundled fork's attribution issue.

This patch wraps the linux x86_64 ly_associate_package call in
both PhysX4 and PhysX5 Gem PAL files with the same
LY_USE_SYSTEM_POLY2TRI gate convention as Patch0006. When the
o3de-rpm spec activates --with system_poly2tri, the gate cmake
falls through to find_package(poly2tri REQUIRED), which is
satisfied by sources/Findpoly2tri-system.cmake (mikkelsen-pattern
shim that bridges the engine's <poly2tri.h> include syntax to
Fedora's /usr/include/poly2tri/poly2tri.h layout via include-path
adjustment).

Linux aarch64 + Mac + Windows are NOT gated here — the system_poly2tri
swap is Linux-x86_64-specific for now (matches the Fedora-track
packaging scope). The aarch64 ly_associate_package line in the
same files stays as the upstream fetcher; future work could
gate it the same way for ARM Fedora packaging.

Carry-patch (applies unconditionally; bundled-poly2tri builds also
benefit from the gate convention being uniform). Activates poly2tri
as a Stage 1 system swap on Fedora packaging — converts the bundle
from "off-limits restricted" to "Stage 1 candidate." Audit-track
analogue of Patch0006's LY_USE_SYSTEM_<X> gates for the standard
BuiltInPackages bundles, applied to PhysX-Gem-internal bundles.

---
--- a/Gems/PhysX/Core/PhysX4/Source/Platform/Linux/PAL_linux.cmake
+++ b/Gems/PhysX/Core/PhysX4/Source/Platform/Linux/PAL_linux.cmake
@@ -18,7 +18,11 @@
 
 if(PAL_TRAIT_BUILD_HOST_TOOLS)
     if(${CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR} STREQUAL "x86_64")
+        if (NOT LY_USE_SYSTEM_POLY2TRI)
         ly_associate_package(PACKAGE_NAME poly2tri-7f0487a-rev1-linux           TARGETS poly2tri PACKAGE_HASH b16eef8f0bc469de0e3056d28d7484cf42659667e39b68b239f0d3a4cbb533d0) 
+        else()
+            find_package(poly2tri REQUIRED)
+        endif()
     elseif(${CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR} STREQUAL "aarch64")
         ly_associate_package(PACKAGE_NAME poly2tri-7f0487a-rev1-linux-aarch64   TARGETS poly2tri PACKAGE_HASH a7dfa76df0b77a65c00e52bda28c3c174fe84ca115f5a015b6e937ee5b55e969)
     else()
--- a/Gems/PhysX/Core/PhysX5/Source/Platform/Linux/PAL_linux.cmake
+++ b/Gems/PhysX/Core/PhysX5/Source/Platform/Linux/PAL_linux.cmake
@@ -18,7 +18,11 @@
 
 if(PAL_TRAIT_BUILD_HOST_TOOLS)
     if(${CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR} STREQUAL "x86_64")
+        if (NOT LY_USE_SYSTEM_POLY2TRI)
         ly_associate_package(PACKAGE_NAME poly2tri-7f0487a-rev1-linux           TARGETS poly2tri PACKAGE_HASH b16eef8f0bc469de0e3056d28d7484cf42659667e39b68b239f0d3a4cbb533d0) 
+        else()
+            find_package(poly2tri REQUIRED)
+        endif()
     elseif(${CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR} STREQUAL "aarch64")
         ly_associate_package(PACKAGE_NAME poly2tri-7f0487a-rev1-linux-aarch64   TARGETS poly2tri PACKAGE_HASH a7dfa76df0b77a65c00e52bda28c3c174fe84ca115f5a015b6e937ee5b55e969)
     else()
